---
import EditorialLayout from '../layouts/EditorialLayout.astro';
import ActionIcon from '../components/editorial/ActionIcon.astro';
import Evidence from '../components/editorial/Evidence.astro';
import TechStack from '../components/editorial/TechStack.astro';
import CareerTimeline from '../components/editorial/CareerTimeline.astro';
import CaseVisual from '../components/editorial/CaseVisual.astro';
import CampaignFigure from '../components/editorial/CampaignFigure.astro';
import { profile, mailto, testimonials } from '../content/editorial.js';
const caseUrl = (id) => `/case-studies/${id}/`;
const recommendations = [testimonials[1], testimonials[2], testimonials[0]];
---
<EditorialLayout home>
  <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="intro-title">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <h1 id="intro-title">I’m Andrew.<br />I like knowing<br /><span>what happens next.</span></h1>
      <p class="intro">Someone clicks an ad. Did they enrol, take out a loan, or place their first order? I’m a paid media specialist who follows those decisions from the ad account into the client’s sales records.</p>
      <p class="hero-detail">I plan and run paid search and social campaigns, build conversion tracking, and use CRM data and sales feedback to decide where the next dollar goes.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href={mailto}>Email Me <ActionIcon name="arrow" /></a><a class="text-link" href={profile.resume} target="_blank" rel="noopener"><ActionIcon name="file" />View résumé</a></div>
      <p class="availability">Available now for hybrid or remote roles in Greater Vancouver</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="portrait-block"><img src="/images/andrew-fonseka-480.webp" srcset="/images/andrew-fonseka-480.webp 480w, /images/andrew-fonseka-720.webp 720w" sizes="(max-width: 380px) calc(100vw - 32px), (max-width: 760px) 300px, (max-width: 1000px) 28vw, 360px" width="480" height="480" alt="Andrew Fonseka, Paid Media Specialist" fetchpriority="high" /><figcaption><strong>Andrew Fonseka</strong><span>Agency experience. In-house perspective.</span><span>Greater Vancouver, BC</span></figcaption></figure>
  </section>
  <div class="proof-strip proof-strip--budget wrap" aria-label="Advertising budget and selected campaign outcomes">
    <a href={caseUrl('aegon')}><strong>Seven-figure</strong><span>annual ad budget<small>Aegon · co-managed with the team</small></span></a>
    <a href={caseUrl('university')}><strong>312</strong><span>fee-paid enrolments<small>Private university · CRM-matched</small></span></a>
    <a href={caseUrl('panasia')}><strong>259</strong><span>funded loans<small>Pan Asia Bank · client-reported</small></span></a>
    <a href={caseUrl('petmart')}><strong>4:1</strong><span>first-order ROAS<small>Petmart.lk · client-reported</small></span></a>
  </div>
  <section id="work" class="wrap chapter two-column">
    <div><p class="dateline">Pan Asia Bank · Colombo · 2023</p>
      <h2>Which enquiries <em>became loans?</em></h2>
      <p class="chapter-intro">At Kites Global, the bank gave me US$25,000 to spend on Gold2Cash. Its sales team had a piece of the puzzle I couldn’t see in either ad account. They were talking to the borrowers.</p>
      <p>Their feedback favoured Meta. I set the split, ran both accounts and reviewed results with the bank. By June, the bank had counted 259 funded loans.</p>
      <CaseVisual campaign="panasia" />
      <a class="read" href="/case-studies/panasia/">Inside the Gold2Cash campaign <ActionIcon name="arrow" /></a>
    </div><CampaignFigure campaign="panasia" />
  </section>

  <section class="agency wrap chapter">
    <p class="dateline">Kites Global · Retail &amp; e-commerce</p>
    <h2>Same agency. <em>Different briefs.</em></h2>
    <p class="chapter-intro">Pan Asia Bank was one of four accounts I managed at Kites Global. For Petmart, the question was how much a first order brought in. For Godrej, it was how to introduce a hair colour to shoppers in India.</p>
    <div class="print-spread">
      <article><CampaignFigure campaign="petmart" /><h3>What was a first order worth?</h3><p>I built Petmart’s Merchant Center feed and split Shopping and Performance Max by new and returning buyers. On US$5,000 in spend, the client reported four dollars in first-order sales for every dollar spent.</p><a class="read" href="/case-studies/petmart/">Read the Petmart figures <ActionIcon name="arrow" /></a></article>
      <article><CampaignFigure campaign="godrej" /><h3>A launch with 30 creators.</h3><p>I helped shape the Godrej Expert Rich Crème launch and ran the Meta and YouTube ads behind the creator programme. Godrej attributed about US$350,000 in sales to paid media that quarter.</p></article>
    </div>
    <p class="marginal"><strong>At the smaller end of my client list</strong> I built a Shopify store and product feed for a Sri Lankan apparel retailer. At about US$850 a month, Shopping and Meta beat its target of 100+ retailer leads by 20%.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="capabilities" class="chapter inhouse"><div class="wrap two-column">
    <div><p class="dateline">Aegon · Canada &amp; U.S. · 2025–26</p><h2>How do you run <em>20 campaigns in a day?</em></h2>
    <p>At Aegon I ran 10–20 campaigns a day and co-managed a seven-figure annual budget. Each launch needed a name the reporting team could use, tracking that worked, and a compliance review.</p>
    <p>I wrote a Google Apps Script builder so the team could turn one brief into a campaign ready for review. Legal and compliance still signed off on every launch.</p>
    <a class="read" href="/case-studies/aegon/">Follow a campaign through the builder <ActionIcon name="arrow" /></a></div>
    <div class="ledger" aria-label="Campaign builder usage"><div><strong>22</strong><span>colleagues used the builder</span></div><div><strong>~200</strong><span>campaigns launched through it</span></div><div><strong>12 days</strong><span>of work saved per year, estimated</span></div></div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="wrap chapter">
    <p class="dateline">Freelance · Education · 2026</p>
    <h2>Two colleges still <em>had seats to fill.</em></h2>
    <div class="two-column">
      <div><p class="chapter-intro">While I was at Aegon, I took on education projects with my employer’s approval. A Saudi university had an intake problem you could easily miss in Ads Manager.</p>
        <p>The broad campaign brought in the cheapest leads, but few of those students enrolled at the two colleges with the most empty seats. I recommended a dedicated Meta campaign for those colleges and helped build and manage it through the partner agency.</p>
        <CaseVisual campaign="university" />
        <a class="read" href="/case-studies/university/">See how admissions counted enrolments <ActionIcon name="arrow" /></a>
      </div><Evidence />
    </div>
    <div class="marginal"><h3>At DIMO Academy, the budget stayed at US$900 a month.</h3><p>I built a landing page and a shorter enquiry form, set up Microsoft Advertising and helped install a chat assistant. The academy counted 212 qualified leads from March to May, up from 178 the quarter before.</p><a class="read" href="/case-studies/dats/">Read about the DIMO rebuild <ActionIcon name="arrow" /></a></div>
  </section>

  <section id="about" class="wrap chapter two-column">
    <div><p class="dateline">About Andrew</p><h2>From Colombo <em>to Vancouver.</em></h2>
      <p>I started at Enfection, supporting campaigns in Sri Lanka, Singapore and Malaysia. By 2023 I was managing four client accounts at Kites Global and supporting five more. I earned my MBA at University Canada West in 2024, then joined Aegon in Langley.</p>
      <p>I’m available now for hybrid or remote paid media specialist and coordinator roles in Greater Vancouver. I speak English and Sinhala and am authorized to work in Canada.</p>
      <div class="story-links"><a href={profile.resume}>Read my résumé (PDF)</a><a href={profile.portfolio}>View the portfolio (PDF)</a></div>
    </div><CareerTimeline />
  </section>

  <TechStack />

  <section class="wrap recommendations chapter" aria-labelledby="recommendations-title">
    <h2 id="recommendations-title">What it’s like to <em>work with me.</em></h2>
    <div class="recommendation-grid">{recommendations.map((t, i)=><figure class:list={["recommendation-card", {"recommendation-featured": i === 0}]} >
      <blockquote><p>“{t.excerpt}”</p></blockquote><figcaption><span class="recommendation-initials" aria-hidden="true">{t.initials}</span><div><strong>{t.name}</strong><span>{t.role}</span></div></figcaption>
      <details><summary>Full recommendation</summary><p>“{t.quote}”</p></details>
    </figure>)}</div>
    <a class="read" href={profile.linkedin + 'details/recommendations/'}>Recommendations on LinkedIn <ActionIcon name="arrow" /></a>
  </section>
</EditorialLayout>
<style is:global>
.editorial .proof-strip--budget { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:0; padding-block:32px; }
.editorial .proof-strip--budget a { display:flex; flex-direction:column; align-items:flex-start; justify-content:flex-start; gap:14px; min-width:0; padding:0 24px; border:0; border-right:1px solid var(--line); }
.editorial .proof-strip--budget a:first-child { padding-left:0; }
.editorial .proof-strip--budget a:last-child { padding-right:0; border-right:0; }
.editorial .proof-strip--budget strong { display:block; font-size:clamp(28px,2.75vw,40px); line-height:1.2; white-space:nowrap; }
.editorial .proof-strip--budget span { display:block; font-size:16px; line-height:1.5; }
.editorial .proof-strip--budget small { display:block; font-size:12px; line-height:1.6; margin-top:6px; }
@media(max-width:1100px) and (min-width:761px) {
 .editorial .proof-strip--budget { grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); padding-block:0; }
 .editorial .proof-strip--budget a { padding:24px; border:0; }
 .editorial .proof-strip--budget a:nth-child(odd) { padding-left:0; border-right:1px solid var(--line); }
 .editorial .proof-strip--budget a:nth-child(-n+2) { border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); }
 .editorial .proof-strip--budget strong { font-size:38px; }
}
@media(max-width:760px) {
 .editorial .proof-strip--budget { grid-template-columns:1fr; padding-block:0; }
 .editorial .proof-strip--budget a, .editorial .proof-strip--budget a:first-child, .editorial .proof-strip--budget a:last-child { display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:8px; padding:24px 0; border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); }
 .editorial .proof-strip--budget a:last-child { border-bottom:0; }
 .editorial .proof-strip--budget strong { font-size:38px; }
}
</style>
